.Dd January 1, 2026
.Dt LEVA-SAMPLE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm leva-sample
.Nd tidy a synthetic collection of widgets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl qv
.Ar widget ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility exists only to exercise the Leva renderer. It reads a list of imaginary
widgets, sorts them by an invented weight, and then pretends to print a summary
of everything it has seen, which is why this paragraph is deliberately long enough
to wrap across several lines at the default width.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl q
Print nothing except the final tally.
.It Fl v
Print one extra line for each widget that was sorted.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
